er 100,000 children aged <15 years per year.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Stool adequacy is defined as having two stool specimens collected ≥24 hours apart and within 14 days of paralysis onset\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"An NPAFP rate ≥2 is considered sufficiently sensitive to detect circulating poliovirus.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"On the basis of the number of nucleotide changes from the closest type 1 virus from Pakistan\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}